@identity.sigil from Identity import { user, actor }
@rooms.sigil from Rooms import {
  room,
  room owner,
  room timezone,
  archived room,
  room lock,
}
@availability.sigil from Availability import {
  open time,
  weekly window,
  blackout,
  slot grid,
  clock,
  nonexistent local time,
  repeated local time,
}

component Booking {
  goal {
    Let a *renter* submit a *booking request* for time on a room and let the
    room owner approve or decline it, without two Confirmed bookings on a room
    ever overlapping.
  }

  interface {
    request lifecycle {
      A renter submits a booking request for a room with a room-local start
      and end in the room timezone. Booking resolves them to a *requested range*
      and records it as Pending or rejects it with a *rejection reason*.

      The room owner approves or declines a Pending booking request on the room.

      A renter withdraws their own Pending booking request.

      The room owner or the renter cancels a Confirmed booking request before
      its requested range starts.

      Booking provides a *range change*, which moves a renter's own Pending
      booking request to a new requested range.
    }

    Booking provides the *availability workflow*, which applies a weekly window
    or blackout change and its sweep in one room lock.

    Booking provides the *archive workflow*, which archives a room with the
    archive sweep, or unarchives it, in one room lock.

    Booking provides the *timezone workflow*, which checks for a Pending or
    Confirmed booking request whose start is after the clock and changes the
    room timezone within one room lock, refusing the change when one exists.

    Booking provides the actor's own booking request list and the inbox of
    booking request items on rooms where the actor is the room owner; every
    item in either list carries its status, any *decline cause*, and its
    derived expired and outside availability flags.

    Booking provides each booking request on a room that overlaps a range, with
    its status, its renter, and its expired and outside availability flags.
  }

  state {
    A booking request is *Pending*, *Confirmed*, *Declined*, *Withdrawn* or
    *Cancelled*.

    Declined, Withdrawn and Cancelled are the terminal booking request
    statuses.

    Booking exclusively owns the archived room mark, since only the archive
    workflow may set or clear it.

    Booking records one decline cause on each Declined booking request:
    declined by owner, overlapping approval, availability change, or archive.

    A requested range is a half-open span of instants that starts and ends on
    the slot grid in the room timezone.

    A Pending booking request whose start is not after the clock is *expired*.
    The expired flag is derived when read and is not a separate status.

    A Confirmed booking request whose start is after the clock and that is not
    wholly inside current open time is *outside availability*. The
    outside availability flag is derived when read.
  }

  logic {
    Booking depends on Availability for open time, and depends on Rooms for the
    room lock and the room owner; every command and query receives the clock
    from its caller.

    submission {
      Submitting takes the actor, the clock, the room and a room-local start
      and end, and opens the room lock for that room.

      It resolves the room-local start and end in the room timezone into the
      requested range, noting any nonexistent local time and resolving a
      repeated local time to its earlier occurrence.

      It checks each rejection reason in the rejection reason order, using the
      clock.

      It then either stops with the first rejection reason or records a Pending
      booking request and returns it.
    }

    approval {
      Approving takes the actor, the clock and a booking request identifier,
      reads the booking request's stored room, and opens the room lock for that
      room.

      It re-loads the booking request and stops unless the actor is the
      room owner, the status is Pending, and the start is after the clock.

      It stops, leaving the booking request Pending, if the requested range is
      not wholly inside current open time.

      It stops with a conflict, leaving the booking request Pending, if the
      no-overlap rule refuses the change to Confirmed.

      It sets the booking request to Confirmed, sets every other overlapping
      Pending booking request on the room to Declined with decline cause
      overlapping approval, and returns the Confirmed booking request.
    }

    Declining, withdrawing and cancelling each take the actor, the clock and a
    booking request identifier, lock the stored room with the room lock,
    re-load the booking request, check the actor and status, change it, and
    return it.

    The availability workflow applies the weekly window or blackout change, then
    sets every Pending booking request whose start is after the clock and that
    is no longer wholly inside open time to Declined with decline cause
    availability change, and returns the result; started and expired items are
    untouched.

    The archive workflow marks the room an archived room, then sets every Pending
    booking request on it to Declined with decline cause archive; unarchiving
    only clears the archived room mark and revives no Declined booking request.
  }

  constraints {
    no-overlap rule {
      Two Confirmed booking request records on the same room must never have
      overlapping requested range values, including under concurrent approvals.

      The database enforces the no-overlap rule with an exclusion constraint on
      Confirmed booking request records, not only application checks.
    }

    The rejection reason order is: own room, archived room, off-grid or
    nonexistent local time, invalid range, start not after the clock, over the
    request limits, outside open time, conflict with a Confirmed
    booking request, and exact duplicate.

    A requested range whose end is not after its start is rejected with the
    invalid range rejection reason.

    The *request limits* are that a requested range must start at most 180 days
    after the clock and last at most 7 days, both measured in room-local calendar
    days and clock times in the room timezone.

    A renter must not hold two Pending booking request records with the same
    requested range on the same room.

    A user must not submit a booking request on a room where that user is the
    room owner.

    Commands on an existing booking request must identify it only by its
    identifier and must derive the room from the stored booking request, never
    from the caller.

    Every status change must be conditional on the expected prior status, and a
    lost race on a Pending booking request must report that it is no longer
    Pending.

    When the room owner or the renter cancels a booking request that is already
    Cancelled, it must succeed without changing it, whichever of them cancelled
    it first.

    A Confirmed booking request that falls outside availability must stay
    Confirmed; availability changes must never cancel a Confirmed booking request.

    Only Booking may write booking request records.

    A room timezone must not change while the room has a Pending or Confirmed
    booking request whose start is after the clock.

    A terminal booking request must never change status.

    Booking must not provide a range change; a renter who wants different time
    withdraws the booking request and submits a new one.

    An expired booking request can still be declined by the room owner or
    withdrawn by its renter, but must not be approved.

    Every future-start, expired and request-limit check on a booking request
    must use the clock and never the database's own notion of now.

    Booking request reads must never be cached; each read reflects the latest
    booking request status.
  }

  decisions {
    Owner approval over instant booking exercises the full booking request
    lifecycle for both the renter and the room owner.

    Only Confirmed booking request records block, so a Pending booking request
    cannot hold a slot; approval clears overlapping Pending ones.

    Expired and outside availability are derived so removing a blackout clears
    the flag with no background job.

    The room timezone is locked while future items exist so no booking request
    ever moves in time.
  }

  cases {
    A Confirmed booking request covers 09:00 to 10:00; a request for 10:00 to
    11:00 is accepted as Pending.

    A Pending booking request starting at 09:00 today is withdrawn by its renter
    at 09:15; it becomes Withdrawn although it is expired.

    The room owner and the renter cancel the same Confirmed booking request at
    the same moment; both are told it is Cancelled and it is cancelled once.

    A requested range from Monday 11:00 to Monday 10:00 is rejected with the
    invalid range rejection reason.

    Weekly hours are Monday 09:00 to 18:00; a requested range Monday 17:30 to
    18:30 is rejected as outside open time.

    Ana and Ben hold Pending booking request records for 13:00 to 15:00 and
    14:00 to 16:00; approving Ana's declines Ben's with decline cause overlapping
    approval.

    A blackout is added over a Confirmed booking request and a Pending one; the
    Confirmed one stays and is outside availability, the Pending one is Declined
    with decline cause availability change.

    Two overlapping Pending booking request records are approved at the same
    moment; exactly one becomes Confirmed.

    The room owner approves while the renter withdraws the same booking request;
    exactly one succeeds and the other is told it is no longer Pending.

    An owner of one room approves a booking request identifier from another room;
    it is refused and neither room changes.

    A blackout that auto-declined a booking request is removed; the
    booking request stays Declined.

    A requested range starting 02:00 on the spring-forward date in
    America/New_York is rejected as a nonexistent local time.

    The room owner tries to change the room timezone while a Confirmed
    booking request is next week; the timezone workflow refuses it.
  }
}
